\viewkind4\uc1\pard\qj\kerning2\f0\fs24 Several officers and dispatchers received commendations for exceptional performance: Emergency Dispatcher Audrey Miranda was honored for expertly coordinating a high-risk perimeter during an armed vehicle theft incident, drawing on her extensive experience to guide multi-agency response and ensure safe apprehension. Officer Breylis Garcia received Officer of the Month for solving a hit-and-run case in which a suspect intentionally ran over a motorcycle officer. Garcia used license-plate technology, cell-site data, and careful evidence preservation to secure charges. Officers Bryan Pita and Rafael Villanueva were recognized for their swift identification and arrest of a vehicle burglary suspect using technology, teamwork, and decisive fieldwork-despite both having less than a year of service. Chief Hudak praised their dedication and highlighted the value of mentoring across generations of officers. \cf1\kerning0\f1\par
}

