\viewkind4\uc1\pard\qj\f0\fs24 The City presented a segment from WPLG Local 10 Television's "Defining Moments in Our Nation's History" series, part of the America's Semiquincentennial Moment initiative, highlighting the women's suffrage movement and its role in expanding civic participation and strengthening American democracy.\cf1\f1\par
}

{\rtf1\fbidis\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fprq2\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ltrpar\qj\f0\fs24 Mayor Lago presented a proclamation declaring June 2, 2026, as Italian National Day (Festa della Repubblica) in Coral Gables. The proclamation marked the 80th anniversary of the June 2, 1946, referendum in which the Italian people voted to establish the Italian Republic - the first time in Italian history that both men and women voted together through universal suffrage, ending the legacy of a totalitarian regime and choosing a democratic path forward. The Italian Consul General addressed the Commission, reflecting on the historic significance of the June 2nd date, noting that Secretary of State Rubio had reaffirmed the day prior that the U.S.-Italy partnership continues to be grounded in shared values of faith, freedom, and the rule of law. He expressed gratitude on behalf of the more than 70,000 Italians residing in Florida, many of whom call Coral Gables home. Mayor Lago thanked the Consul General for his active engagement in city life beyond official diplomatic functions, noting that Italy serves as a model he regularly references when recruiting other consulates to establish a presence in Coral Gables. He also thanked the City's ACM and DCM for their coordination in organizing the event. Commissioner Fernandez welcomed the Consul General in Italian, noting that Italy is the country with which Coral Gables shares the most cultural and aesthetic commonality, given the Mediterranean architectural tradition that defines the city.\cf1\f1\par
}

